<div class="detail-copy">
<h2>Project overview</h2>
<p>This project explores Learning from Demonstration (LfD) for robotic manipulation. The goal is to use demonstrations collected through a leader-follower robotic setup as data for training and evaluating policies that reproduce a task.</p>
<h2>Engineering activities</h2>
<ul class="clean-list">
<li>Use of a leader-follower robotic system to collect demonstrations.</li>
<li>Recording and organization of robot observations and actions.</li>
<li>Exploration of imitation-learning approaches for manipulation tasks.</li>
<li>Evaluation of trained policies through robotic execution.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Technologies</h2>
<p>SO-ARM101, LeRobot, Python and machine-learning-based imitation learning.</p>

